==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-reformation.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[improvement]] (or an intended improvement) in the existing form or [[condition]] of institutions or practices etc.; intended to make a [[striking]] [[change]] for the better in social or political or religious affairs.
#* '''1625''', {{w|Francis Bacon}}, "Of Innovation"
#*: It is good also, not to try experiments in states, except the necessity be urgent, or the utility evident; and well to beware, that it be the '''reformation''', that draweth on the change, and not the desire of change, that pretendeth the '''reformation'''. 
#* '''1677'', {{w|John Dryden}}, ''The State of Innocence and the Fall of Man'', Aurthor's Apolgy:
#*: {{...}} satire lashes vice into '''reformation''', and humour represents folly so as to render it ridiculous.

